          </c>
          <c capture="False" background="#F3F7F8" formula="RouteLength"><num>12.376 ft</num></c>
        </row>
      </table>
    </embed>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Negative return setback means the cap footprint overlaps the wall line; it is not a 24-in front-wall pass. The selected layer is below the cap, so the cap projection is shown but not treated as an obstruction at that layer. No vertical detour through/under the cap is calculated.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Current landing wall interior angles are 90 deg. Layer and local wall H are checked at the anchor. The wall envelope is conservatively retained along the entire route without taking credit for wall height steps. Vendor development length, opposing reinforcement interference, connection width/edge offsets and full backfill domain require separate detailing.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="12" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" textcolor="#1766A0">STEP 4 OF 4 | USE AND LIMITATIONS</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Edit common controls on the first tab. Expand EditableGeometry here for wall lines, panel thickness, pile sizes and layer offsets. Walls must remain parallel to the sheet axes; rotated-wall inputs are rejected. Recalculate in Blockpad. Inspect both signed routes and the all-origin table after each change.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">A source snapshot is not an approved as-built survey. Geometry outputs are unfactored lengths and angles. Plumb-pile plan clearance does not verify 24-in battered-pile-to-leveling-pad clearance at depth. Set VendorReady only when the trial inputs have been confirmed.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="3"><dynexp formula="ReviewState = If(Basis.VendorReady,&quot;INPUTS MARKED CONFIRMED - GEOMETRY SCREEN ONLY&quot;,&quot;REVIEW - VENDOR INPUTS UNCONFIRMED&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showresult="True" showformula="True"><expbody>ReviewState = If(Basis.VendorReady,"INPUTS MARKED CONFIRMED - GEOMETRY SCREEN ONLY","REVIEW - VENDOR INPUTS UNCONFIRMED")</expbody><expresult> = REVIEW - VENDOR INPUTS UNCONFIRMED</expresult></dynexp></paragraph>
  </report>
  <report name="EB2" title="03 - End Bent 2" unit="in" pagesize="816,1056" margin="48,48,48,48" bordermargin="0,0,0,0" collapsemargins="False">
    <stylerule type="AnyEquation" name="Input" texthighlight="#F7E6B9"/>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="14" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold">END BENT 2 | PILE / MSE PLAN</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Dimensions in feet unless shown otherwise. Strap begins at the BACK of facing, perpendicular projection of selected pile center. Plan is live; positive sheet y points into the approach.</paragraph>
    <section name="RouteControls" capture="False" hide="false">
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="3"><dynexp formula="WallChoice = 1" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showresult="True" showformula="True" style="Input"><expbody>WallChoice = 1</expbody><expresult> = 1.000</expresult></dynexp></paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Wall: 1 front, 2 left return, 3 right return.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="3"><dynexp formula="PileChoice = 2" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showresult="True" showformula="True" style="Input"><expbody>PileChoice = 2</expbody><expresult> = 2.000</expresult></dynexp></paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Selected pile: 1 through 4, left to right.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="3"><dynexp formula="Direction = 1" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showresult="True" showformula="True" style="Input"><expbody>Direction = 1</expbody><expresult> = 1.000</expresult></dynexp></paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Selected drawing sign: +1 or -1 relative to wall tangent.</paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="3"><dynexp formula="LengthOverride = 0 ft" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showresult="True" showformula="True" style="Input"><expbody>LengthOverride = 0 ft</expbody><expresult> = 0.000 ft</expresult></dynexp></paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" spacingafter="5" textcolor="#43505C">Zero uses ordinary minimum from local H. Enter longer vendor design length here.</paragraph>
    </section>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="12" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" textcolor="#1766A0">STEP 1 OF 4 | PLAN AND SELECTED ROUTE</paragraph>
