    </embed>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Extra d is added wall-normal separation needed to clear the TARGET at 15 degrees, with current width/gap/tolerance. It is a geometric sensitivity, not a proposed wall relocation; recheck all piles, walls and cap after changing layout.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="12" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" textcolor="#1766A0" pagebreakbefore="Break">STEP 3 OF 4 | CAP / LENGTH / LAYER</paragraph>
    <embed spacingbefore="5" spacingafter="8">
      <table name="Separate" capture="False" colwidths="1:340, 2:190">
        <stylerule range="A1:B8" fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="9" border="Border(&quot;AllSides&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.6, &quot;#A7B9C6&quot;); Border(&quot;BetweenRows&quot;, &quot;Solid&quot;, 0.4, &quot;#CBD5DD&quot;);"/>
        <stylerule range="A1:B1" background="#DCE7F3" fontweight="bold"/>
        <row>
          <c capture="False" background="#DCE7F3">
            <textvalue>Independent check</textvalue>
          </c>
          <c capture="False" background="#DCE7F3">
            <textvalue>Live result</textvalue>
          </c>
        </row>
        <row>
          <c capture="False" background="#F3F7F8">
            <textvalue>Front cap face to back of front panel</textvalue>
          </c>
          <c capture="False" background="#F3F7F8" formula="CapSetback1 to in"><num>24.617 in</num></c>
        </row>
        <row>
          <c capture="False" background="#F3F7F8">
            <textvalue>Front setback requirement</textvalue>
          </c>
          <c capture="False" background="#F3F7F8" formula="FrontCapStatus"><textvalue>PASS</textvalue></c>
        </row>
        <row>
          <c capture="False" background="#F3F7F8">
            <textvalue>Cap signed setback from left return</textvalue>
          </c>
          <c capture="False" background="#F3F7F8" formula="CapSetback2 to in"><num>-1.974 in</num></c>
        </row>
        <row>
          <c capture="False" background="#F3F7F8">
            <textvalue>Cap signed setback from right return</textvalue>
          </c>
          <c capture="False" background="#F3F7F8" formula="CapSetback3 to in"><num>-2.027 in</num></c>
        </row>
        <row>
          <c capture="False" background="#F3F7F8">
            <textvalue>Strap layer elevation</textvalue>
          </c>
          <c capture="False" background="#F3F7F8" formula="Basis.Layer"><num>38.000 ft</num></c>
        </row>
        <row>
          <c capture="False" background="#F3F7F8">
            <textvalue>Cap soffit elevation</textvalue>
          </c>
          <c capture="False" background="#F3F7F8" formula="CapBottom"><num>40.250 ft</num></c>
        </row>
        <row>
          <c capture="False" background="#F3F7F8">
            <textvalue>Selected route length</textvalue>
          </c>
          <c capture="False" background="#F3F7F8" formula="RouteLength"><num>12.751 ft</num></c>
        </row>
      </table>
    </embed>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Negative return setback means the cap footprint overlaps the wall line; it is not a 24-in front-wall pass. The selected layer is below the cap, so the cap projection is shown but not treated as an obstruction at that layer. No vertical detour through/under the cap is calculated.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Current landing wall interior angles are 90 deg. Layer and local wall H are checked at the anchor. The wall envelope is conservatively retained along the entire route without taking credit for wall height steps. Vendor development length, opposing reinforcement interference, connection width/edge offsets and full backfill domain require separate detailing.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="12" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" textcolor="#1766A0">STEP 4 OF 4 | USE AND LIMITATIONS</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Edit common controls on the first tab. Expand EditableGeometry here for wall lines, panel thickness, pile sizes and layer offsets. Walls must remain parallel to the sheet axes; rotated-wall inputs are rejected. Recalculate in Blockpad. Inspect both signed routes and the all-origin table after each change.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">A source snapshot is not an approved as-built survey. Geometry outputs are unfactored lengths and angles. Plumb-pile plan clearance does not verify 24-in battered-pile-to-leveling-pad clearance at depth. Set VendorReady only when the trial inputs have been confirmed.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="3"><dynexp formula="ReviewState = If(Basis.VendorReady,&quot;INPUTS MARKED CONFIRMED - GEOMETRY SCREEN ONLY&quot;,&quot;REVIEW - VENDOR INPUTS UNCONFIRMED&quot;)" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showresult="True" showformula="True"><expbody>ReviewState = If(Basis.VendorReady,"INPUTS MARKED CONFIRMED - GEOMETRY SCREEN ONLY","REVIEW - VENDOR INPUTS UNCONFIRMED")</expbody><expresult> = REVIEW - VENDOR INPUTS UNCONFIRMED</expresult></dynexp></paragraph>
  </report>
  <report name="RouteMath" title="04 - Geometry method" unit="in" pagesize="816,1056" margin="48,48,48,48" bordermargin="0,0,0,0" collapsemargins="False">
    <stylerule type="AnyEquation" name="Input" texthighlight="#F7E6B9"/>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="12" spacingafter="5" fontweight="bold" spacingbefore="8" keepwithnext="True" textcolor="#1766A0">STRAIGHT-STRIP GEOMETRY</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">At the back of facing the anchor lies exactly on the normal through the selected pile center. Let d be center distance normal to wall, a the pile half-size normal to wall plus location allowance, b the tangential half-size plus allowance, and r = strap width / 2 + required clear gap.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">At skew theta, the signed near-corner distance from the ray is (d-a) sin(theta) - b cos(theta). A target clears when this distance is at least r, the pile is ahead of the wall, and the strap reaches beyond the pile. The drawings and full-route check use finite segments; the target-angle equation describes the continuing ray.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Required target angle = ATan[b/(d-a)] + ASin[r/Sqrt((d-a)^2+b^2)]. Invalid domains are rejected. The square enclosing the slightly rotated source pile is conservative. Finite segment-to-rectangle distance is zero on intersection; otherwise it is the minimum endpoint-to-rectangle or rectangle-corner-to-segment distance.</paragraph>
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">A full-route PASS means one tested sign clears all modeled obstacles at that angle, length and layer. A full-route FAIL means neither tested sign works. Unless the target-angle check also fails, other angles within 15 degrees may still work; adjust TestAngle. No dog-leg, strap bending, attaching to a pile, or change of connection position is assumed.</paragraph>
    <section name="GeometryFunctions" capture="False" hide="true">
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="3"><dynexp formula="Safe(x) = If(Abs(x) &lt; 0.000000001 ft, 0.000000001 ft, x)" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showresult="False" showformula="True"><expbody>Safe(x) = If(Abs(x) &lt; 0.000000001 ft, 0.000000001 ft, x)</expbody></dynexp></paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="3"><dynexp formula="Clamp(x) = Min(1,Max(0,x))" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showresult="False" showformula="True"><expbody>Clamp(x) = Min(1,Max(0,x))</expbody></dynexp></paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="3"><dynexp formula="Low(a,b,p,q) = If(Abs(q) &lt; 0.000000001 ft, If(And(p &gt;= a,p &lt;= b),-1000000000,1000000000),Min((a-p)/Safe(q),(b-p)/Safe(q)))" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showresult="False" showformula="True"><expbody>Low(a,b,p,q) = If(Abs(q) &lt; 0.000000001 ft, If(And(p &gt;= a,p &lt;= b),-1000000000,1000000000),Min((a-p)/Safe(q),(b-p)/Safe(q)))</expbody></dynexp></paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="3"><dynexp formula="High(a,b,p,q) = If(Abs(q) &lt; 0.000000001 ft, If(And(p &gt;= a,p &lt;= b),1000000000,-1000000000),Max((a-p)/Safe(q),(b-p)/Safe(q)))" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showresult="False" showformula="True"><expbody>High(a,b,p,q) = If(Abs(q) &lt; 0.000000001 ft, If(And(p &gt;= a,p &lt;= b),1000000000,-1000000000),Max((a-p)/Safe(q),(b-p)/Safe(q)))</expbody></dynexp></paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="3"><dynexp formula="PointRect(x,y,a,b,c,d) = Sqrt(Max(a-x,0 ft,x-b)^2+Max(c-y,0 ft,y-d)^2)" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showresult="False" showformula="True"><expbody>PointRect(x,y,a,b,c,d) = Sqrt(Max(a-x,0 ft,x-b)^2+Max(c-y,0 ft,y-d)^2)</expbody></dynexp></paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="3"><dynexp formula="Part(x,y,p,q,u,v) = Clamp(((x-p)*(u-p)+(y-q)*(v-q))/Max((u-p)^2+(v-q)^2,0.000000000001 ft^2))" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showresult="False" showformula="True"><expbody>Part(x,y,p,q,u,v) = Clamp(((x-p)*(u-p)+(y-q)*(v-q))/Max((u-p)^2+(v-q)^2,0.000000000001 ft^2))</expbody></dynexp></paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="3"><dynexp formula="PointSeg(x,y,p,q,u,v) = Sqrt((x-p-Part(x,y,p,q,u,v)*(u-p))^2+(y-q-Part(x,y,p,q,u,v)*(v-q))^2)" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showresult="False" showformula="True"><expbody>PointSeg(x,y,p,q,u,v) = Sqrt((x-p-Part(x,y,p,q,u,v)*(u-p))^2+(y-q-Part(x,y,p,q,u,v)*(v-q))^2)</expbody></dynexp></paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="3"><dynexp formula="Dist(p,q,u,v,a,b,c,d) = If(Max(0,Low(a,b,p,u-p),Low(c,d,q,v-q)) &lt;= Min(1,High(a,b,p,u-p),High(c,d,q,v-q)),0 ft,Min(PointRect(p,q,a,b,c,d),PointRect(u,v,a,b,c,d),PointSeg(a,c,p,q,u,v),PointSeg(a,d,p,q,u,v),PointSeg(b,c,p,q,u,v),PointSeg(b,d,p,q,u,v)))" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showresult="False" showformula="True"><expbody>Dist(p,q,u,v,a,b,c,d) = If(Max(0,Low(a,b,p,u-p),Low(c,d,q,v-q)) &lt;= Min(1,High(a,b,p,u-p),High(c,d,q,v-q)),0 ft,Min(PointRect(p,q,a,b,c,d),PointRect(u,v,a,b,c,d),PointSeg(a,c,p,q,u,v),PointSeg(a,d,p,q,u,v),PointSeg(b,c,p,q,u,v),PointSeg(b,d,p,q,u,v)))</expbody></dynexp></paragraph>
      <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="1" spacingbefore="3"><dynexp formula="Needed(d,a,b,r) = If(Or(d &lt;= a,r &gt;= Sqrt((d-a)^2+b^2)),90 deg,ATan(b/Max(d-a,0.000000001 ft))+ASin(Min(1,r/Max(Sqrt((d-a)^2+b^2),0.000000001 ft))))" mathlayout="on" showsteps="False" showresult="False" showformula="True"><expbody>Needed(d,a,b,r) = If(Or(d &lt;= a,r &gt;= Sqrt((d-a)^2+b^2)),90 deg,ATan(b/Max(d-a,0.000000001 ft))+ASin(Min(1,r/Max(Sqrt((d-a)^2+b^2),0.000000001 ft))))</expbody></dynexp></paragraph>
    </section>
  </report>
</document>
